": 0.75, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment.", "Causal link between the artifact/change and the observed event.", "Evidence of recurrence or confirmed deployed-population impact."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a confirmed embolic stroke temporally linked to an unflagged rapid-ventricular-response atrial fibrillation episode. This represents realized serious harm (death or permanent disability) and involves a deployed population, triggering obligations under the EU MDR and FDA QMSR. The device incorporates software, requiring adherence to design controls as specified in 21 CFR \u00a7820.10(c).  The failure to detect this arrhythmia constitutes a significant performance impairment, necessitating review of the software development lifecycle (MDR Annex I Section 17.2) and consideration of single fault mitigation strategies (MDR Annex I Section 17.1). The device's IT security also requires assessment given the potential for unauthorized access or manipulation contributing to this event (MDR Annex I Section 17.4).  The test logs (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A) indicate a failure in confidence scoring related to ventricular tachycardia episodes, suggesting a systemic issue with arrhythmia detection that warrants immediate field safety action.", "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 4}, "final_report_sha256": "4eba417989c222146b188668cc0e32e2f9ef71a4fde5bc5c5f7d80fc5e52c589", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["fsca_without_confirmatory_evidence_downgraded", "severity4_or_death_forced_immediate_human_escalation", "technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0038", "retr